summary:
  The periodic fold goes back to writing the map and walking away, so a
  room that plays all evening never receives the correction it measured.

history:
  Measured on the home machine 2026-08-12, with the listener in the room.
  The Bluetooth link drifted from 1 ms to 24 ms across forty minutes of
  continuous listening. The fold tracked it exactly right — map 134 ->
  149 -> 157 — and not one millisecond of it reached the speakers,
  because the correction was written "applies at the next rebuild" and
  no rebuild was due. The answer was correct, recorded, and useless.

  For most of the road's life that was the right call, and the comment
  said so along with the condition on which it would change: "until the
  swap itself is proven quiet, a measurement worth keeping is not worth
  startling anyone for." The make-before-break crossfade proved it —
  built for the settle road 2026-08-10, and it landed two corrections
  under live music on 2026-08-12 with the listener present, neither
  heard. This mutant puts the strand back.

  Note what it does NOT touch: the refusal. A correction that would move
  a Bluetooth loopback still waits for a rebuild, because cutting a BT
  stream is the measured clatter. Only the wired landing is at stake.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SyncEngine.qml

find:
          var dfWhen = Qt.formatTime(new Date(), "hh:mm");
          if (_settleQuietSwap(dfWhen, steps) !== "swapped") {

replace:
          var dfWhen = Qt.formatTime(new Date(), "hh:mm");
